    "lines": [
      {
        "snippetId": "s988",
        "messageOrdinal": 61,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1845-07-18",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "18 July 1845",
        "text": "Yesterday you must have wondered at me for being in such a maze altogether about the poems--and so now I rise to explain that it was assuredly the wine song and no other which I read of yours in Hood's.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s2359",
        "messageOrdinal": 153,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1845-11-21",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "21 November 1845",
        "text": "And it made me glad ... happy--perhaps too glad and happy--and surprised: yes, surprised!--for if you had told me (but you would not have told me) if you had let me guess ... just the contrary, ...",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s5616",
        "messageOrdinal": 292,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-03-31",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "31 March 1846",
        "text": "You, on the other side, never overstate anything ... never enlarge ... never exaggerate!",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s5660",
        "messageOrdinal": 293,
        "sender": "Robert",
        "date": "1846-04-01",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "1 April 1846",
        "text": "The ‘good’ you do me, I see you cannot see nor understand yet—there is my answer!",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s6608",
        "messageOrdinal": 331,
        "sender": "Robert",
        "date": "1846-04-27",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "27 April 1846",
        "text": "Rastignac, Mme. d’Espard, Desplein &c.—they keep alive, moving—it is not ingenious?",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s6779",
        "messageOrdinal": 339,
        "sender": "Robert",
        "date": "1846-05-02",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "2 May 1846",
        "text": "Moxon told me Tennyson was still in Town.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s7601",
        "messageOrdinal": 378,
        "sender": "Robert",
        "date": "1846-05-28",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "28 May 1846",
        "text": "Ah, there will be time to contrive, to concert—but the worst is that when I see you I contrive nothing, nor do you help me, you Ba!",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s8463",
        "messageOrdinal": 416,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-06-22",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "22 June 1846",
        "text": "How did you get home? how are you, dearest?",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s9307",
        "messageOrdinal": 450,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-07-10",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "10 July 1846",
        "text": "I have walked out to-day, you did me so much good yesterday.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s10921",
        "messageOrdinal": 511,
        "sender": "Robert",
        "date": "1846-08-21",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "21 August 1846",
        "text": "Do you understand all this, Ba?",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s11972",
        "messageOrdinal": 548,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-09-08",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "8 September 1846",
        "text": "Does not that sound like ‘a grave woman?’",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s12099",
        "messageOrdinal": 556,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-09-12",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "12 September 1846",
        "text": "Was I very uncourteous to your cousin?",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      }
    ]
  }
}
